align "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Gates: 59" [:br {}] "Length: 1200 m" [:br {}] "Start Altitude: ?" [:br {}] "Vertical Drop: 400 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The women’s giant slalom made its Olympic début with this event, the first Alpine event at the 1952 Winter Olympics. It was contested as a single run, as was the men’s, and the women would not have two runs in the giant slalom at the Olympics until " [:a {:href "/results/1339"} "1980"] ". At the 1950 World Championships, the winner was Austrian " [:a {:href "/athletes/82216"} "Dagmar Rom"] ", with her teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/80622"} "Trude Jochum-Beiser"] ", who would win the " [:a {:href "/results/1199"} "downhill in Oslo"] ", placing second in Aspen."] "\n\n" [:p {} "However, the winner by a large margin in Oslo was " [:a {:href "/athletes/81799"} "Andrea Mead-Lawrence"] ", who would add a second gold medal in the " [:a {:href "/results/1201"} "slalom"] " a few days later. Rom placed second, but Jochum-Beiser struggled to a tie for 11th. The bronze medalist was Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/80745"} "Mirl Buchner"] ", who would win three Alpine medals in Oslo – bronze in slalom and giant slalom, and silver in the downhill. Rom later had a minor career as an Austrian actress in films."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/81799"} "Andrea Mead-Lawrence"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:06.8"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "9"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/82216"} "Dagmar Rom"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "